          "List SubTitle 2": "Project Type",
          "Heading 1": "INTRODUCTION",
          "Description 1": "Bruno was designed to be more than just a personal portfolio \u2014 it\u2019s a statement piece for creative professionals. Whether you\u2019re a designer, developer, or digital artist, Bruno gives you the canvas to showcase your skills in a bold and minimalist way. The client wanted a design that was sharp, responsive, and easy to navigate, while also standing out in a crowded digital space.\n",
          "Heading 2": "DESIGNING METHOD",
          "Description 2": "We focused on a grid-based layout with powerful visual rhythm. Strong typography, clean sections, and a modular design system make it easy to plug in new work or tweak the aesthetic. The site\u2019s animations brought life to the transitions \u2014 scroll effects, fade-ins, and micro-interactions added personality without distraction.\n",
          "Description 3": "The color palette is restrained and modern, keeping the spotlight on the work itself. We used generous spacing, custom project cards, and interactive hover states to keep users engaged as they browse. The goal was to make the portfolio feel like a curated experience, not just a listing of work.\n",
